@Gateway_HostAddress = http://localhost:5000
@access_token = YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

# ========================================
# Error Handling & Standardization (US-52)
# ========================================
# The Gateway provides consistent error responses with:
# - Standard format: { statusCode, message, details, source, timestamp }
# - Proper HTTP status codes (400, 401, 502, 504, etc.)
# - Gateway errors distinguished by "source": "Gateway"
# - Circuit breaker (passive health checks) with 1-minute reactivation
# - Automatic failover when downstream services fail
#
# Error Response Example:
# {
#   "statusCode": 502,
#   "message": "Service unavailable",
#   "details": "Unable to reach downstream service",
#   "source": "Gateway",
#   "timestamp": "2026-05-06T10:30:00Z"
# }

# ========================================
# Load Balancing Configuration (US-51)
# ========================================
# The Gateway now supports load balancing with:
# - Round-robin distribution across multiple instances
# - Active health checks every 30 seconds
# - Automatic removal of failed instances
#
# To add more instances, edit appsettings.json Clusters section:
# "Destinations": {
#   "service-api-1": { "Address": "http://localhost:5001" },
#   "service-api-2": { "Address": "http://localhost:5011" }
# }

### Gateway Health Check
GET {{Gateway_HostAddress}}/health
Accept: application/json

###

# ========================================
# US-43: Auth Service Routes via Gateway
# ========================================

### Auth Service Health Check (GET)
GET {{Gateway_HostAddress}}/api/auth/health
Accept: application/json

###

### Register New User (POST) - Public endpoint
POST {{Gateway_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "Test123!@#",
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "User"
}

###

### Login User (POST) - Public endpoint
# Save the token from response to use in protected endpoints
POST {{Gateway_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "Test123!@#"
}

###

### Get User by Email (GET) - Public endpoint
GET {{Gateway_HostAddress}}/api/auth/users/test@example.com
Accept: application/json

###

# ========================================
# US-46: JWT Authentication on Gateway
# ========================================

### Test Protected Endpoint WITHOUT Token (Should return 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{Gateway_HostAddress}}/api/notifications
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "type": "info",
  "title": "Test Notification",
  "message": "This should fail without a token"
}

###

### Test Protected Endpoint WITH Valid Token (Should succeed)
# First login above to get a token, then paste it in @access_token variable
POST {{Gateway_HostAddress}}/api/notifications
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "userId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "type": "info",
  "title": "Test Notification",
  "message": "This should succeed with valid token"
}

###

### Get Notification WITH Token
GET {{Gateway_HostAddress}}/api/notifications/123456
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

###

# ========================================
# US-44: Projects Service Routes via Gateway
# (Now requires JWT authentication)
# ========================================

### Upload Image WITH Token (POST with file - Large file upload support)
# Note: Replace with actual file path for testing
POST {{Gateway_HostAddress}}/api/images/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
X-User-Id: 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="test-image.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./path/to/your/test-image.jpg
------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW--

###

# ========================================
# US-45: Notifications Service Routes via Gateway  
# (WebSocket and API now require JWT authentication)
# ========================================

### WebSocket Status Check WITH Token
GET {{Gateway_HostAddress}}/api/websocket/status
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

###

# WebSocket Connection (Use with WebSocket client or JavaScript)
# Connect to: ws://localhost:5000/api/websocket/connect?access_token=YOUR_JWT_TOKEN
# JavaScript example:
# const ws = new WebSocket('ws://localhost:5000/api/websocket/connect?access_token=' + token);
